{
  "name": "Notify – Discord + Email",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Notify – Discord + Email\n\n### How it works\nA small sub-workflow that other workflows call to send one alert to Discord and/or email.\nInputs: `subject`, `message` (plain text) and `html` (optional email body). Discord messages are cut to Discord's 2,000-character limit.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a **Discord Webhook** credential (Server settings → Integrations → Webhooks) and an **SMTP** credential, and select them on the two send nodes.\n2. In **⚙️ Config** turn each channel on or off and set the email addresses.\n3. Click **Test workflow** on *▶ Send a test alert* to check both channels.\n4. **Publish** it (n8n 2.x only calls published sub-workflows; on 1.x Activate is optional).\n\nDon't set *Error Handler – Alert On Failed Workflows* as this workflow's own error workflow: a failing alert would call itself in a loop.",
        "height": 601,
        "width": 500
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -620,
        -360
      ],
      "id": "31ff2ba9-3250-598c-89c8-07b21f350899",
      "name": "📘 About"
    },
